# Voltage: postpone the Dolby Media C2 HAL start until boot has completed.
#
# The stock declaration lives in the Sony blobs
# (vendor/sony/extra/audio/proprietary/vendor/etc/init/vendor.dolby.media.c2@1.0-service.rc,
# installed as /vendor/etc/init/vendor.dolby.media.c2@1.0-service.rc) and has no
# 'disabled' attribute, so init's "on boot" class_start hal launches it in the
# middle of early codec scanning. On a fresh flash the binary dies with SIGSEGV
# there almost every boot, and system_server cascade-restarts if it hits the
# dead window. Same binary, same user/group/ioprio/writepid, no seclabel (the
# SELinux domain is derived from the binary path and does not change), plus
# 'override' + 'disabled': class_start hal skips it (init StartIfNotDisabled()),
# and the explicit trigger below starts it once sys.boot_completed=1.
#
# 'class hal' is deliberately NOT carried over the stock declaration:
# vndservicemanager.rc has 'onrestart class_restart hal' WITHOUT the
# --only-enabled flag, and Service::Restart() -> Start() clears SVC_DISABLED,
# so an early vndservicemanager restart before boot_completed could start this
# service ahead of the trigger. Out of the hal class the service is unreachable
# from class_start/class_restart, while init's normal crash-restart (Reap()) and
# the explicit trigger still work as intended.
#
# /vendor/etc/init/*.rc files are imported alphabetically (Parser::ParseConfigDir
# std::sort) and init honours the LAST declaration of a service that carries the
# 'override' option (ServiceParser::EndSection removes the earlier one), so this
# file must sort after vendor.dolby.media.c2@1.0-service.rc.

service vendor-dolby-media-c2-hal-1-0 /vendor/bin/hw/vendor.dolby.media.c2@1.0-service
    override
    disabled
    user mediacodec
    group camera mediadrm drmrpc
    ioprio rt 4
    writepid /dev/cpuset/foreground/tasks

on property:sys.boot_completed=1
    start vendor-dolby-media-c2-hal-1-0
